# - Record lines 183-195: the figures are credited to the wrong run. The check (lens-check.mjs, STEP = 2) sampled 62,500 of 250,000 pixels; its files print 288, 5,966 and 1,278 pixels, and 0.3% past white at both strengths on NIR_1376. The listed full-density figures (1,186, 24,091, 5,233 and the rest) come from the instrument lens's rerun. Say so where they appear.
# - Record lines 184-185: the added capture line in `__jpsCapture` calls renderOffscreen, overrides Renderer.HIST_MAX, reads pixels back and restores the default framebuffer, so it renders as well as reads. Reword; the six identical hashes remain the evidence it left the output alone.
# - Record lines 191-192: cite the per-pixel GPU comparison (99.9 to 100% of pixels within 3 levels), not only the box means, which a mirrored-row plant passes. The Not-tested list at line 240 onward should not also claim the pixel-by-pixel comparison was untested; settle which is right.
