# - Record lines 229-231: "none of the drop" holds with the balance stepped as the slider steps it (-0.3%, 0.0%, +0.4%). Unstepped gives -5.5%, +7.1% and -0.4%; the 7.1% on NIR_3716 is dropped.
# - Record lines 233-235: name the pixel set. The low-end clamp red was measured on the mechanism lens's wider paling set (saturation falls by 0.15 or more with value 0.7 or more at 1: 8.1%, 71.0% and 26.9% of the crop), where a channel is below 0 before the tone clamp on 19.3%, 2.0% and 5.9% at strength 0 and none at 1. On the record's whitening class, 0% are below 0 at tap 11. NIR_3700's band-guard amplification is the same: median band gain 1.600 to 1.030 on the wider set, 1.6 on the strict set.
# - Record lines 235-236: "43 to 58%" is two values (43% at strength 0, 58% at 1), not a range. Also missing: on NIR_3700 the lens strength moves the sky selection itself (a gains-only reconstruction on the strength-0 sky maps differs from the strength-1 render by a median 0.035 through the sky stages), which matters to 069 and 023, both of which read the sky selection.
# - Record, missing finding (caveats or "What it supports"): across the whole crop, strength 1 carries MORE green and blue past white before the clamp on all three raws (sampled: NIR_1376 G 70 to 142, B 38 to 74; NIR_3716 G 24 to 137, B 46 to 304; NIR_3700 G 1,169 to 2,642, B 1,385 to 2,452). At full resolution 241, 47 and 2,366 pixels are newly past white at 1, nearly all near-neutral at 0. Clip control does not answer the whitening foliage, but this is what it guards and what 069's cloud is made of; without the line, option 1 reads as irrelevant to 069.
# - Record lines 150-151 and 244-245, and NOTES.md lines 1105-1106: 5 to 7% goes past every measurement. Blue over red 0.936, 0.947 and 0.936 is a cut of 5.3% to 6.4%. Use about 5 to 6%, or 5 to 6.5%.
# - Record lines 152-153: low saturation explains the size of the move, not its direction. Add that after white balance blue is the highest channel and red the lowest on 95%, 100% and 97% of these pixels, so cutting blue against red moves them toward white. Also add, in option 6 or the caveats, that at the raw stage (tap 0) saturation RISES at strength 1 by a factor of 1.03 to 1.04 on all three raws, so tap 2 is only the first place white is defined; this bears on option 6's open question.
